{% doc %}
  PDP delivery information block (strategy decision 2026-06-12):
  honest sticker price + transparent delivery BEFORE checkout. Shows the
  UK rates, the delivery estimate, and the returns promise.

  Delivery estimate: PawScout writes a per-product order->door range (calendar
  days, e.g. "6-21") into supplier.delivery_days from the synced CJ logistics
  matrix. When present it's shown verbatim; when blank (stale / not yet synced)
  a conservative static window is shown. Rule: only surface what is real and
  defensible — the synced figure when we have it, a conservative window otherwise.

  NB: rates below mirror Shopify Settings → Shipping. If the rates change
  there, update these assigns (single source kept deliberately simple —
  Liquid cannot read shipping settings).
  @param {product} product - Product being viewed
{% enddoc %}

{%- liquid
  assign free_threshold = 5000
  assign standard_rate = '£4.99'
  assign delivery_days = product.metafields.supplier.delivery_days.value
-%}

<div class="delivery-info" aria-label="Delivery information">
  <ul class="di-rows">
    <li>
      <strong>FREE UK delivery</strong> on orders over {{ free_threshold | money }}
    </li>
    <li>
      Standard delivery {{ standard_rate }} &middot; estimated
      {%- if delivery_days != blank %} {{ delivery_days }} days{%- else %} 8-21 days{%- endif %}
    </li>
    <li>
      14-day returns &middot; <a href="/policies/refund-policy">see our returns policy</a>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
